  "answer": "This is a known crash: a NullReferenceException in BindingExpression.SetupDefaultValueConverter, thrown while WPF handles a system theme change (ThemeManager.OnSystemThemeChanged). It has been reported many times across versions, and the past tickets were closed as duplicates of the tracking issue PowerToys#37859, so follow that issue for any fix. The past tickets offer no workaround or fix. Your report matches them, so please add any details you have to #37859, such as what you were doing when it crashed (for example waking from sleep, switching light/dark mode, or locking and unlocking the PC). The crash comes from WPF's theme-change handling, so avoiding theme changes while PowerToys is running might reduce how often it happens, but the tickets do not confirm this."
